pos/celery/celery/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/deployments","created_at":"2009-04-24T11:31:24Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T11:08:53Z","pushed_at":"2026-03-10T15:04:28Z","git_url":"git://github.com/celery/celery.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:celery/celery.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery","homepage":"https://docs.celeryq.dev","size":36397,"stargazers_count":28268,"watchers_count":28268,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4989,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":773,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["amqp","python","python-library","python3","queue-tasks","queue-workers","queued-jobs","redis","redis-queue","sqs","sqs-queue","task-manager","task-runner","task-scheduler"],"visibility":"public","forks":4989,"open_issues":773,"watchers":28268,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/pulls/9774","html_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/9774","diff_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/9774.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/9774.patch","merged_at":"2025-06-24T05:39:09Z"},"body":"## Description\r\n\r\n<!-- Please describe your pull request.\r\n\r\nNOTE: All patches should be made against main, not a maintenance branch like\r\n3.1, 2.5, etc.  That is unless the bug is already fixed in main, but not in\r\nthat version series.\r\n\r\nIf it fixes a bug or resolves a feature request,\r\nbe sure to link to that issue via (Fixes #4412) for example.\r\n-->\r\n(Fixes #9773)\r\n\r\nWhen using chords with a group containing failing tasks and a chain body, error propagation fails with:\r\n```\r\nValueError: task_id must not be empty. Got None instead.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis happens because the chord body can be frozen with `None` as its task ID, causing error handling to break when trying to propagate failures from the group to the callback.\r\n\r\n### Root Cause\r\n\r\nIn `celery/canvas.py`, the `_chord.run()` method was freezing the body with a potentially `None` task_id:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# BEFORE (problematic):\r\nbodyres = body.freeze(task_id, root_id=root_id)  # task_id can be None!\r\n```\r\n\r\n**The issue:**\r\n- `task_id` can be `None` when chord is called without explicit ID\r\n- When a group task fails, error handling looks for `callback.id` to propagate the error  \r\n- Since the body was frozen with `None`, `callback.id` ends up being `None`\r\n- This causes the \"task_id must not be empty\" error during error storage\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\n\r\nEnsure the chord body always gets a valid, unique task ID while maintaining proper group relationships:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# AFTER (correct):\r\nbody_task_id = task_id or uuid()\r\nbodyres = body.freeze(body_task_id, group_id=group_id, root_id=root_id)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Why this is correct:**\r\n- **Fixes the immediate issue**: Body always has a valid ID for error handling (never `None`)\r\n- **Maintains uniqueness**: Each task gets its own Redis storage key (no collisions)\r\n- **Preserves relationships**: Body is properly linked to the group via `group_id` parameter\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\nThe fix includes tests covering:\r\n- Error propagation with different chord body types (single task, chain, group, chord)\r\n- Proper task ID generation when none is provided\r\n- Verification that body tasks get unique IDs while maintaining group membership\r\n- Integration tests ensuring no regression in existing functionality","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/9774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/9774/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":18240500071,"node_id":"REFE_lADOAALQjM68bvVMzwAAAAQ_N_Fn","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/events/18240500071","actor":{"login":"dfm88","id":71150812,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMTUwODEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71150812?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm88","html_url":"https://github.com/dfm88","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm88/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm88/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm88/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm88/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfm88/subscriptions","organizati